DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ll22ccoonnttrrooll utility connects to the local device with the specified
     BD_ADDR or name and attempts to send the specified command.  The
     ll22ccoonnttrrooll utility will print results to the standard output and error
     messages to the standard error output.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa _l_o_c_a_l
             Connect to the local device with the specified BD_ADDR or name.
             Example: --aa 00:01:02:03:04:05 or --aa bt_device.

     --hh      Display usage message and exit.

     --nn      Show Bluetooth addresses as numbers.  Normally ll22ccoonnttrrooll attempts
             to resolve Bluetooth addresses, and display them symbolically.

     _c_o_m_m_a_n_d
             One of the supported commands (see below).  The special command
             hheellpp can be used to obtain a list of all supported commands.  To
             get more information about a specific command use hheellpp _c_o_m_m_a_n_d.

     _p_a_r_a_m_e_t_e_r_s
             One or more optional space separated command parameters.

